hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"175","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I have been given five things which were not given to any prophet before me: the entire earth has been made a mosque and a means of purification for me; I have been helped by instilling fear into the enemy; spoils of war have been made lawful for me; I have been sent to both the red and the white (i.e., all mankind); and I have been granted intercession.”"
"176","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The whole earth is a place for prayer except for the bathhouse and the graveyard."""
"177","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best rows for men are the first ones and the worst are the last ones, (whereas) the best rows for women are the last ones and the worst are the first ones."""
